    <mxCell id="legend_bg" value="" style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F8FAFC;strokeColor=#CBD5E1;strokeWidth=1.5;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="35" y="1055" width="2050" height="130" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
    <mxCell id="legend_title" value="Legend &amp; Invariants" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;fontSize=12;fontStyle=1;fontColor=#0F172A;fontFamily=Helvetica;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="49" y="1061" width="2022" height="22" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
    <mxCell id="legend_text" value="1. Evaluation order: Center firewall evaluates top-down (CC-GST explicit denies before allows; CC-DEF-01 default deny logged); Cloud uses TGW routes + NACLs + SGs + endpoint policies.&lt;br/&gt;2. Zero AWS Network Firewall &amp; no NAT GW (CL-EGR-01): centers enter private endpoints via static IKEv2 IPsec; internet ingress only via IoT mTLS and WAF front doors.&lt;br/&gt;3. Temporary rules (Audit): CC-LNK-06/CL-LNK-05 (QA acceptance), CC-ADM-05 (maintenance windows), CC-ADM-06 (commissioning laptop .60). Permanent rules coded in Epic 6.&lt;br/&gt;4. Solid blue/green = permanent allow; dashed amber = temporary/backup; dashed red = explicit deny or blackhole; dashed grey = reserved empty or not deployed." style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#334155;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacingTop=2;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="49" y="1083" width="2022" height="98" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
  </root>
</mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
